      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "Forecast Weather Influences: A dry day with strong to gale force South backing South-South-East winds. The freezing level will be around 900 metres.\nObserved Weather Influences: A dry day with strong to gale force South-Easterly winds.  The freezing level at midday was around 900 metres.\nObservedSnowStability: New windslab has developed on West to North aspects mainly above 1000 metres. Although poorly bonded these accumulations are mostly isolated, and in some areas localised. Areas especially affected are steep locations such as coire rims and the tops of gullies.  The avalanche hazard is Low."
